-- CR-064 — new Ontology concept type `service-name`. Owner: "They have to
-- come from the ontology layer... This service code turn-around-time-high
-- can be declared in development pack and deployment pack with different
-- service levels" — two different Packs deliberately declaring the same
-- code as the same canonical concept only works if the code itself is a
-- shared, governed vocabulary term, not free text each Pack author might
-- spell differently. Freely-extensible, same pattern as `capability-name`/
-- `feature-flag` (plain Ontology CRUD, no graduated-entity lineage tracking
-- like `deliverable-name` needed — CR-049 graduated that one out of plain
-- CRUD specifically for Draft->Active lineage, which nothing here requires).
--
-- Seeded with every real Service code the 22 clean-slate-exercised Pack
-- files (plus the 3 confirmed-dead ones, same "kept for consistency" CR-061
-- gave Policy's own non-exercised files) already declare live — 124 real,
-- distinct codes — so the Ontology-backed validation this CR adds doesn't
-- reject any of them.
ON CONFLICT (concept_type, code, tenant_id) DO NOTHING;
